WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.260
VINCE: Hey, I've Vince.

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.300
JOHNNY: I'm Johnny.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.800
We're the co-founders of
Social Talent here in Dublin.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.630
VINCE: We actually met in the
Cayman Islands in an Irish bar,

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.610
as one does.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.430
And Johnny made a proposition
that I would make millions

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.184
from setting up a
recruitment agency.

00:00:14.184 --> 00:00:16.350
JOHNNY: Within six months
we'd burned all our money.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.790
We had young kids.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.050
And we said, you know what?

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.450
Maybe there's a
business in teaching

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.560
people a new way of recruiting.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.720
VINCE: Everything that we
did was quite different.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.094
JOHNNY: Each user
on our platform

00:00:27.094 --> 00:00:30.330
gets access to a gamified
learning platform with lots

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.240
of content and best practices,
short microlearning videos,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.550
tips on how to use
social media tools, web

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.930
tools, different ways
to be more productive.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.920
It's like Netflix for HR
recruiting professionals.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.836
VINCE: Actually, you can
scrap the rest of it.

00:00:42.836 --> 00:00:44.690
That's the answer.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.670
JOHNNY: So one day I get a call
from one of our team saying,

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.890
Johnny, what you
need this money for?

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.980
What do you mean, what
do I need this money for?

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.190
She sends me a copy of
an e-mail I apparently

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.607
had sent her, saying I
needed her to send me funds.

00:00:56.607 --> 00:00:58.440
Then two minutes later,
I got another e-mail

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.020
from somebody else, a customer,
saying what's this all about?

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.170
I'm the CEO of the
company, and my mail

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.535
is used to go to lots of people.

00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:07.530
And this was a disaster.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.002
I go down to one of
my colleagues to say,

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:11.460
we need to fix
this, this is crazy.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.450
How do we do it?

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:17.040
Within a few minutes, she got
in contact with our Google team,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.890
and within a few hours,
we had gotten a code

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.690
from the guys in support.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.140
And all of a sudden, the
whole thing was resolved.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.760
I didn't expect as
a small business

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.900
that we'd get that support.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.490
It was a huge surprise, a huge
comfort to me to get that.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.990
The reputational damage of
that could have been massive.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.490
It just takes one
or two customers

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.640
to believe that was us.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.320
For Google to come and help us
like that within a few hours--

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.500
that's priceless.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.000
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:49.156 --> 00:01:51.030
VINCE: I would like say
that I do get e-mails

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.600
from Johnny asking for money.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.470
And I don't believe
they're spoofs.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.430
And, try as I
might, I don't think

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.810
Google will be able to help me.

